+# Changes since the first release (Nov 2026)
+
+The product repos changed a lot after the KPIs were first written. This section is what was re-read and what the KPIs now do.
+Repos read: PAY, PMS, DESK (the former CYBER repo), Chama, Register.
+
+## PAY: new money products and a new rent fee model
+
+| Charge type | Reference | Where | Revenue (company) | Notes |
+|-------------|-----------|-------|-------------------|-------|
+| Plot Yangu rent (new model) | `INV_` | `transactions/{ref}` | `platformKeptMinor` (net); revenue = `chargeMinor - netPayoutMinor`; pass-through = `agentMinor`; gateway = `paystackFeeMinor` | The tenant pays rent plus a capped fee; the landlord pays a tier-based convenience % (0.2 enterprise, 0.4 pro, 0.65 business, 0.95 otherwise); the desk agent shares the convenience. PAY now records the books on the transaction. Older payments fall back to the earlier rules |
+| Lipa Mos Mos instalment | `LMM_` | `lmm_payments` | surcharge; net = `keptMinor` | Minor units, `createdAt` epoch ms. Credited to the landlord, settled in transfers |
+| Lipa Mos Mos settlement fee | - | `lmm_settlements.chunks[]` | `feeMinor` minus `paystackCostMinor` on successful chunks | Revenue-only line |
+| Lipa Mdogo Mdogo instalment | `LMX_` | `lmmx_payments` | service fee + reserve; pass-through = `deskShareMinor`; net after Paystack fee | Tenant plan with desk agents sharing the service fee |
+| Lipa Mdogo Mdogo transfer cost | - | `lmmx_ledger` type `payout_fee` | negative (real Paystack transfer cost) | Balances the reserve collected at instalment time |
+| Lipa Mdogo Mdogo withdrawal fee | - | `lmmx_ledger` type `withdraw_service` | positive | Revenue-only line |
+| Landlord Watch transcript | `LWT_` | `platform_revenue` type `landlord_watch_transcript` | `netRevenue` | KES 99 per extra transcript |
+| Compliance report | `CRP_` | `platform_revenue` type `compliance_report` | `netRevenue` | KES 200 |
+
+"Revenue-only" lines count in GMV, fees, revenue and net revenue but not in attempts, success or the success rate, so those stay a pure view of customer checkouts.
+New revenue streams: `instalments`, `transfers`, `withdrawals`, `lookups`. New charge types are listed in `collectors/pay/facts.ts`.
+Not counted: Perks (a loyalty points ledger, no company revenue), and the desk commission split on SMS top-ups (the desk share is not recorded on the top-up record yet, so Register and Plot Yangu SMS net revenue is slightly overstated when a desk is involved).
+
+## Plot Yangu (PMS)
+
+- **SMS credits are `users.tokens`**, not `messageTokens` (the earlier KPI read the wrong field; `messageTokens` is Register's name). `pms.tokens_outstanding` is corrected.
+- **Tiers are free, low, business, solo, pro, enterprise.**
+- **SMS usage is now measurable** from `users/{uid}/sms-sent-log` (`recipientCount`, `successCount`, `failCount`, `tokensCharged`, `sentAt`). The text and phone numbers are never selected.
+- Tenants and invoices created by DESK sit in the same `users/{u}/tenants|invoices` paths and are counted with the rest.
+
+## DESK (Cyber)
+
+| KPI group | Collection | Fields |
+|-----------|------------|--------|
+| WhatsApp usage (exact) | `whatsapp_usage/{day}` | The meter is deployed in DESK; unchanged |
+| House to Rent | `houseInquiries` | `status` (sent or failed), `credits`, `ownerId`, `createdAt` Timestamp |
+| Desk network flows | `desk_events` | `paidAt` epoch ms, `type` (refund excluded from sales), `product` (chama, school, pms), `agentId`, `grossMinor`, `feeMinor`, `agentSharePct` |
+| Desk network stock | `desk_agents` (`rank`, `status`), `desk_customers` | Aggregate counts only |
+
+Desk commission is derived: `(grossMinor - feeMinor) x agentSharePct / 100`. The money itself moves inside the Paystack split.
+The platform id stays `cyber` in data; labels say DESK.
+
+## Unchanged and re-checked
+
+Chama (same collections, plan ids, `ourFee` and `paystackFee` fields) and Register (same collections) needed no change.
